<p>Doug's other inventory is fertilizer, seed and fuel. The cash cost is the same as the <abbr title="fair market value">FMV</abbr> for this inventory. Its value is as follows:</p> <ul>
<li>bought in his <span class="nowrap">2024 fiscal</span> period: $15,000</li>
<li>bought in his <span class="nowrap">2023 fiscal</span> period:   $6,000</li>
<li>bought in his <span class="nowrap">2022 fiscal</span> period:   $5,000</li>
</ul> <p>At the end of his <span class="nowrap">2024 fiscal</span> period, Doug did not have any other inventory that he bought before his <span class="nowrap">2021 fiscal</span> period.</p>
<p>Doug has registered his livestock under the <a href="https://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/A-11.2/index.html" rel="external">Animal Pedigree Act</a>. He wants to designate these animals as specified animals. Doug fills in <span class="nowrap">chart 1</span> as follows:</p>
<p class="text-center"><strong>Chart 1<br/> Cash cost of purchased inventory</strong></p>
